C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:204:### 2.8 Prompt-stack guide reflection / benchmark maintenance
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:209:- benchmark question generation, self Q/A, answer verification, and patch / rerun loops are the real work
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:221:- `PROMPT_tool_protocol_overlay` when OCR, MCP, or tool-mediated capability inspection materially changes evidence quality
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:222:- `PROMPT_guardrails_safety_overlay` when disclosure, mutation, or approval risk changes the benchmark path
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:225:- `Benchmark registry memo` for chapter-family inventory, cohort scope, or expected packet floor
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:226:- `Guide reflection benchmark memo` for question -> answer -> verification -> patch-target loops
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:227:- `Prompt-stack release review` when the benchmark is deciding release, rewrite acceptance, or parity preservation
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:229:- `Context sufficiency review memo` or `Critique quality review memo` when weak context or no-gain iteration may explain benchmark instability
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:234:- document-benchmark to assembled-replay escalation
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:235:- route choice between staying document-grounded vs escalating to behavior proof
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:237:Default route policy for this maintenance class:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:238:- primary route: stay at document-level benchmark while the live question is doc/runtime parity, chapter-family answerability, or benchmark coverage
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:239:- fallback route: escalate to assembled replay when ambiguity, conflict, or behavior-critical claims need stronger evidence than document-grounded review can provide
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:240:- final ownership reroutes to `eval-ops` once the decision depends on replay execution state, benchmark gating, or release-sensitive continuation rather than route comparison alone
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:243:- for `runtime owner integrity` and `benchmark-loop adequacy`, document-level benchmark is the primary sufficient surface when runtime-owned docs directly expose the owner boundary or benchmark loop
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:244:- replay escalation is not required for those families unless the claim extends from document/runtime parity into assembled behavior proof or runner execution state
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:246:Escalate to stronger operational artifacts when:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:247:- document parity is no longer the live question and assembled prompt behavior must be replayed
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:248:- scenario lineage, run linkage, or replay execution state must stay inspectable across reruns
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:249:- the verdict depends on whether a replay actually executed rather than whether a benchmark question set exists
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:251:Preferred operational artifacts:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:252:- `Benchmark cohort manifest` when scenario identity and expected replay contract must be fixed before execution
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:253:- `Replay runner verdict sheet` when runner state, partial completion, or replay-attempted vs replay-complete distinction is the live issue
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:254:- `Replay suite verdict memo` when a higher-level suite verdict must summarize multiple runner-linked replay outcomes without hiding partial coverage
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:265:- route choice under budget or risk -> `Resource budget and route-choice memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:270:- retrieval boundary or mode escalation -> `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:274:- blocked state or controlled fallback -> `Recovery / escalation checkpoint memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:282:- approval-sensitive execution -> `HITL approval packet` or `Plan approval checkpoint artifact`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:285:- process-quality or replay-safe inspection -> `Safe trajectory artifact report`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:289:- guide-chapter reflection or doc-to-runtime parity benchmark -> `Guide reflection benchmark memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:290:- assembled prompt replay setup -> `Benchmark cohort manifest`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:291:- assembled prompt replay runner-state verdict -> `Replay runner verdict sheet`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:292:- assembled prompt replay suite summary -> `Replay suite verdict memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:294:- versioned replay suite or benchmark cohort definition -> `Benchmark registry memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:298:- route, prioritization, or exploration scoring -> `Route-quality scorecard`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:299:- repo-scale coding scenario and verification-running contract -> `Coding benchmark scenario memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:300:- executed benchmark result or cohort verdict -> `Benchmark execution report`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:301:- replay execution verdict -> `Replay suite verdict memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:305:- route-switch and re-prioritization audit -> `Route re-prioritization audit memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:307:- integrated promotion packet with confidence class -> `Release evidence bundle v2`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:309:- benchmark cohort identity and run-linkage packet -> `Benchmark cohort manifest`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:310:- replay execution-sheet and runner linkage packet -> `Replay runner verdict sheet`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:314:- route-switch benchmark packet -> `Route-switch benchmark verdict`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:315:- coding execution-ledger packet -> `Coding benchmark execution ledger`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:320:- release-gate attachment set -> `Release evidence bundle memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:324:When Codex is maintaining reflection against a governing guide, use these anchor routes:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:326:- Prompt Chaining / Planning -> base prompts; keep staged dependency, checkpoint, and fallback visibility explicit instead of collapsing into one-shot execution language
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:327:- Routing / Prioritization / Exploration -> `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo` or `Prioritization queue / next-action memo`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:332:- Retrieval / RAG -> `PROMPT_retrieval_grounding_overlay` + `grounded-research`; prefer `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo` or `Source consultation ledger`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md:333:- Resource-Aware Optimization -> base prompts plus `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`; prefer `Resource budget and route-choice memo`
