C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:209:## 7. Base Skill Routing Rules
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:211:Use no skill by default if the task is tiny and the direct path is already safe and obvious.
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:213:Load one primary skill when the task materially matches its domain.
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:214:Load at most one secondary skill only when the gain is real and the overlap is clean.
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:216:Primary skills available in this project:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:219:- `design-analysis`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:225:- Document-grounded investigation / latest facts / source-backed answer / evidence synthesis -> `grounded-research`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:226:- Architecture / design trade-offs / option comparison / strategic technical decision -> `design-analysis`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:230:Skill loading rules:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:231:- do not load a skill merely because it exists
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:232:- do not load multiple heavy skills when one clearly fits
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:234:- prefer no skill over a weakly matched skill
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:235:- if the task changes materially, reroute
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\AGENTS.md:264:- if blast radius rises materially, slow down and make the risk explicit
