C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:6:# Design Analysis Skill
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:8:This skill is the primary execution pack for high-value design and analysis tasks.
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:32:Use this skill when one or more apply:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:37:- the task is high-risk, ambiguity-heavy, or dependency-heavy
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:41:Do not use this skill when:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:44:- the task is mostly evidence collection rather than decision-making
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:46:- the real question has already become benchmark gating, replay continuation, or prompt-stack release judgment rather than route comparison; reroute primary ownership to `eval-ops`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:54:- exposing trade-offs and risk
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:55:- keeping cost, latency, and operating budget visible when they can change the recommendation
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:60:This skill temporarily elevates from the base coding constitution toward `full`-style depth when the task earns it.
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:69:- route quality materially affects the result
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:71:- failure cost is high
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:81:`Clarify Goal -> Frame Problem -> Define Constraints -> Generate Small Candidate Set -> Compare -> Choose Route -> Plan / Recommend -> Verify -> Finalize`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:84:`Clarify -> Decompose -> Gather Evidence -> Compare -> Critique -> Refine Recommendation -> Finalize`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:92:- if multiple comparison tracks run in parallel, define the join artifact and evaluation owner before fan-out
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:101:- risk tolerance
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:109:- define the strongest observable solved condition, such as one recommended path, one fallback, and one validation direction when relevant
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:112:- prioritize the comparison move that reduces the highest-risk uncertainty first
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:120:- one conservative / low-risk path
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:129:- high-cost without compensating value
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:132:- one best path plus one fallback
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:142:- cost
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:156:- if cost, latency, or operating budget can change the winner, keep those axes visible
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:158:- if the recommendation depends on bounded parallel work, keep `parallelism cap`, `join cost`, and `saturation risk` visible enough that coordination overhead is part of the comparison rather than hidden execution drag
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:159:- if the recommendation remains provisional, keep one cheaper fallback path and one stronger-route trigger visible
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:162:Guide-reflection route rule:
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:163:- when the live question is whether to stay at document-level benchmark or escalate to assembled replay, this skill may compare the routes
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:164:- default primary recommendation is document-level benchmark while the question is still doc/runtime parity, chapter-family answerability, or benchmark coverage
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:165:- default fallback recommendation is assembled replay escalation when ambiguity, conflict, or behavior-critical claims need stronger proof than document-grounded review can provide
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:166:- once the question becomes benchmark gating, replay execution state, or release-sensitive continuation, reroute final ownership to `eval-ops`
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:167:- an explicit reroute to `eval-ops` counts as the direct ownership-preserving answer path for this skill; do not force replay-verdict language from route-comparison prose alone
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:168:- do not let route-comparison prose impersonate benchmark or replay verdict authority
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:178:- risk-aware
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:186:- rollback or fallback thoughts
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:194:- prefer a fixed evaluation route over discovery-heavy planning
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:198:- if the recommended path would trigger destructive, costly, or policy-sensitive execution, present the plan for review before recommending autonomous execution
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:205:- resource budget and route-choice memo
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:207:- recovery / escalation checkpoint memo when blocked comparison state or fallback selection becomes the real control surface
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:209:- evidence target / retrieval-mode memo when route quality depends on grounded acquisition strategy
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:210:- source consultation ledger when the recommendation depends on which source groups were actually consulted or how public/private evidence was blended
C:\WORK\0.穈𨰰𥘵\PROMPT\prompt-stack\v32\codex\skills\design-analysis\SKILL.md:212:- release evidence bundle memo when a recommendation must be attached to an actual promotion or hold decision
